  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual material as the 'person' initiating the interaction",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material ('hey, i just met you...') which frames the user as the 'person' who just met someone and is offering a number for camping. This projection is implicit through the first-person perspective of the text, which the user identifies with when viewing the meme. The user is not explicitly deictic (e.g., 'me' or 'you'), but the text's casual, conversational tone and the meme's structure create a direct identification with the speaker of the text, making the user the 'you' in the scenario. The user is projected onto the text_chunk entity.",
